Equivalence Groups Found
└── finite-state machine engine for modeling controller states/transitions
    ├── Candidates : transitions, python-statemachine, fysom, automat
    ├── Used APIs  : Machine, add_transition, conditions, after, wildcard transitions 
    │   ('*'), model-injected state attribute
    ├── Pitfalls   : transitions injects the FSM behavior directly into an arbitrary 
    │   model object (self); python-statemachine and automat require class-based 
    │   declarative definitions (State objects, decorators) instead of imperative 
    │   add_transition calls; fysom uses a config-dict driven initialization 
    │   (events/callbacks keyed by name) rather than add_transition method calls, 
    │   requiring restructuring of guard/callback wiring; automat (Twisted) uses a 
    │   completely different decorator-based state/input/output model with no direct 
    │   concept of 'conditions' or 'after' strings; wildcard source transitions ('*') 
    │   are a transitions-specific convenience; other libraries require explicit 
    │   enumeration of all source states or different syntax; guard functions 
    │   (can_fill) and callbacks (open_inlet, etc.) are referenced by string name in 
    │   transitions; alternatives often want callables or decorated methods, forcing 
    │   rewrites of the guard/callback wiring
    ├── Constraints: requires_connector
    └── The file uses `transitions.Machine` bound to `self` as a model, with 
        `add_transition` calls that reference guard/callback methods by string name and
        support wildcard source states. python-statemachine, fysom, and automat are all
        general-purpose FSM libraries that could conceptually replace transitions for 
        encoding TankController's states and guarded transitions, matching the 
        discovery step's suggestions. However none of them share transitions' exact 
        'model injection + string-referenced conditions/after + add_transition() 
        imperative API' style.

