│    34     success. minimalmodbus.Instrument opens its serial port immediately       │
│    35     upon construction (via the constructor's `port` argument) and has no      │
│    36     separate connect() method -- the port is either already open or gets      │
│    37     reopened automatically around each transaction. This wrapper is           │
│    38     therefore a no-op unless the client exposes its own serial handle,        │
│    39     in which case it makes a best effort to (re)open it, mirroring the        │
│    40     "ensure connected" intent of the original pymodbus call.                  │
│    41     """                                                                       │
│    42     serial_port = getattr(client, "serial", None)                             │
