  ⚠ Remaining incompatibilities noted by connector LLM:
    - aiomqtt.Client is async-only and must be used as an async context manager (`async
with`); there is no synchronous, persistent-connection equivalent to paho's 
Client()/connect()/publish() pattern used throughout _default_client and MqttSink.
    - client.connect(host, port) (used in _default_client right after Client() 
construction) has no aiomqtt equivalent — aiomqtt takes hostname/port at construction 
and connects only upon entering the async context manager, which cannot be faithfully 
reproduced by a synchronous wrapper without effectively re-implementing an event loop 
lifecycle around every call.
    - self.client.publish(...) in MqttSink.publish is called synchronously and its 
return value is inspected via getattr(info, 'rc', 0); aiomqtt's publish() is a 
coroutine returning None on success (raising on failure) rather than an object with an 
.rc attribute, so the whole sync call-and-inspect-rc pattern has no direct analog.
    - The overall design relies on a sync/callback execution model that aiomqtt does 
not support; forcing compatibility would require converting MqttSink and its call sites
to async, which is a structural rewrite beyond glue-code wrapping.

